<h2>Why are concert tickets so expensive once fees are added?</h2>
<p>Service and processing fees help cover payment processing, customer support, platform maintenance and security. Most ticket revenue goes to the organizers, performers and promoters, while marketplaces provide the platform that connects buyers and sellers.</p>
<p>At Seat Outlet, ticket prices and fees are shown during checkout, and you pay the total shown. Compare totals, not just the first number you see.</p>

<h2>Why are concert tickets so expensive on resale marketplaces?</h2>
<p>Ticket holders who cannot attend may resell, and on a marketplace the seller sets the price. That means a resale ticket can cost more than face value for a hot show, and less than face value when demand is soft. Seat Outlet does not set seller prices and does not promise the lowest price.</p>
<p>For background on the concept, see this overview of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ticket_resale" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ticket resale</a>. Policies on resale money for artists or organizers vary by event and region.</p>

